# SDD Harness — outbound channel webhooks
#
# Copy this file to ~/.env.channels and fill in the webhook URLs you want.
# Then lock it down:   chmod 600 ~/.env.channels
#
# This file lives in your HOME directory — NOT inside any git repo — so the
# credentials physically cannot be committed. Configure only the platforms you
# use; the rest are skipped silently. With no file present, /notify and the
# daily report are clean no-ops.
#
# ── Where to get each URL ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Slack   : Create app → Incoming Webhooks → Add New Webhook to Workspace.
#           https://api.slack.com/messaging/webhooks
# Discord : Server Settings → Integrations → Webhooks → New Webhook → Copy URL.
# Teams   : Channel → ⋯ → Workflows → "Post to a channel when a webhook request
#           is received" (Power Automate). Older tenants: ⋯ → Connectors →
#           Incoming Webhook.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
TEAMS_WEBHOOK_URL=
